  md5('reading' || '|' || 'Based on the second paragraph, why is telling a teenager to simply go to bed earlier likely to have limited effect?')::UUID,
  md5('reading' || '|' || 'Why does the author bring up school districts that moved their start times later?')::UUID,
  md5('reading' || '|' || 'Taking both paragraphs together, what pattern do the ancient and modern Olympics share?')::UUID,
  md5('reading' || '|' || 'Why does the author give the number of athletes and nations at the 1896 Athens Games?')::UUID,
  md5('reading' || '|' || 'What does the second paragraph suggest would most likely have happened if one company had owned the internet''s protocols?')::UUID,
  md5('reading' || '|' || 'Why does the author include the estimate that about a third of the world''s people have never been online?')::UUID,
  md5('reading' || '|' || 'Based on the passage, why can a fall in a community''s vaccination rate endanger someone who cannot be vaccinated at all?')::UUID,
  md5('reading' || '|' || 'Why does the author bring up smallpox at the end of the passage?')::UUID,
  md5('reading' || '|' || 'What does the second paragraph suggest about why so many rivals kept suing Bell''s company?')::UUID,
  md5('reading' || '|' || 'How does the second paragraph of this passage relate to the first paragraph?')::UUID,
